<Heading>UK Visa Information</Heading>

FOSS4G 2027 takes place in **Bristol, United Kingdom** from **23 to 29 August 2027**. 

*Depending on your nationality, you may need either an **Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA)** or a **Standard Visitor visa** to attend.*

<Card title="Check your visa requirements" color="secondary">
  <p class="m-0">The quickest way to find out what applies to you is the UK government's <a href="https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa">Check if you need a UK visa</a> tool.</p>
</Card>


*We provide this information for general guidance only and are not liable if it is incorrect or incomplete. If you are not sure, please check the information on the GOV.UK website*

<h3 class="text-2xl font-light">British and Irish Citizens</h3>
        <p>
          If you are a <strong>British or Irish citizen</strong>, you do not need a visa or an ETA to travel to the UK.
        </p>
        <p>
          You also do not need an ETA if you already have a <strong>UK visa</strong> or <strong>permission to live, work or study in the UK</strong>.
        </p>


<main class="my-4 space-y-5">

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 space-y-4 pb-4 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:space-y-0 sm:space-x-4">

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-4 sm:flex-col">

      <section>
        
      </section>

      <section>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Visa Required</h3>
        <p>
          If you are not eligible for an ETA, you will need to apply for a <strong>Standard Visitor visa</strong> before you travel.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cost</strong>: £135 for up to 6 months</li>
          <li><strong>Earliest application</strong>: 3 months before you travel</li>
          <li><strong>Decision</strong>: usually within 3 weeks</li>
          <li>You will need to attend a <strong>visa application centre</strong> to provide your fingerprints and photo</li>
        </ul>
        <Button href="https://www.gov.uk/standard-visitor">Standard Visitor visa</Button>
      </section>

    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-4 sm:flex-col">

      <section>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-light">Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA)</h3>
        <p>
          Visitors who do not need a visa, including those from <strong>Europe, the USA, Australia, Canada</strong> and certain other countries, must get an <strong>ETA</strong> before travelling to the UK.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cost</strong>: £20</li>
          <li><strong>Apply</strong>: using the UK ETA app or online</li>
          <li><strong>Decision</strong>: usually within 1 day, but allow up to 3 working days</li>
          <li><strong>Valid for</strong>: 2 years, or until your passport expires if sooner</li>
          <li>Every traveller needs their own ETA, including babies and children</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Only apply through GOV.UK or the official UK ETA app. Be aware that other websites may charge more.
        </p>
        <Button href="https://www.gov.uk/eta">Apply for an ETA</Button>
      </section>

    </div>

  </div>

</main>

<Card title="Visa support for FOSS4G 2027 attendees">
  <p class="m-0"> 
  The FOSS4G 2027 organisers will be able to issue a <b>letter of invitation</b> to registered attendees to support a Standard Visitor visa application. Details of how to request a letter will be published here once registration opens.
  <br />
  As visa applications can be made up to <b>3 months before you travel</b>, we recommend that attendees who need a visa apply as early as possible, from late May 2027.
  <br />
  If you have any questions, please contact us at <a href="mailto:info@foss4g.org">info@foss4g.org</a>.
  </p>
</Card>

## Useful links

- [Check if you need a UK visa](https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa)
- [Get an electronic travel authorisation (ETA)](https://www.gov.uk/eta)
- [Apply for an electronic travel authorisation (ETA)](https://www.gov.uk/guidance/apply-for-an-electronic-travel-authorisation-eta)
- [Standard Visitor visa](https://www.gov.uk/standard-visitor)
- [Apply for a Standard Visitor visa](https://www.gov.uk/standard-visitor/apply-standard-visitor-visa)

UK immigration rules and fees can change. Please always check the latest guidance on [GOV.UK](https://www.gov.uk/browse/visas-immigration) before you travel.


